<%# locals: (item:) %>

<%# What the customer chose, and nothing else: extras, ingredients at a portion
    they asked for, and their notes. The standard recipe is not a choice they
    made, so printing it back at them is noise. Cancelled items get nothing,
    since describing food nobody received only makes them hunt for a charge.

    Kept in step with Receipt::Bill through Receipt::Components, which is the one
    definition of how a component is described. %>
<% unless item.cancelled? %>
  <% Receipt::Components.new(item).each_label(modified_only: true) do |label| %>
    <div class="text-xs text-muted-foreground ml-6"><%= label %></div>
  <% end %>

  <% if item.special_notes.present? %>
    <div class="text-xs text-muted-foreground ml-6 italic"><%= item.special_notes %></div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
